-- title:
--   Boundary Bernoulli expansion of a face-cut correlation
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite with decidable equality and let $S$ be a face-regularity state on $G^{j+1}$. For every real-valued $f$ and cut-test family $u$, the residual face-cut correlation equals the sum over Boolean boundary assignments $b$ of $\mathrm{boundaryBernoulliWeight}(u,b)$ times the Boolean cut correlation on the support of $b$. The identity holds without a boundedness assumption on $u$.
